{title: Morning Road}
{artist: Songlivo example}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse}
[G]Coffee on the [C]window, [G]sun is coming [D]up
[Em]Packing up the [C]car with an [G]old tin [D]cup
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Take the morning [G]road, [D]let the radio [Em]play
[C]Every song we [G]know [D/F#]carries us a[G]way
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Mile after [C]mile and the [G]map's in the [D]back
[Em]Nobody's in a [C]hurry, we [G]never look [D]back
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge}
[Am]Slow down, [C]there's no clock to [D]beat
[Am]Windows down, [C]drumming on the [D]seat
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Take the morning [G]road, [D]let the radio [Em]play
[C]Every song we [G]know [D/F#]carries us a[G]way
{end_of_chorus}
